{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GFhS2s5d7bCdas7s9c6M9M","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd110-pr\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/pr: Paginate or Columnate Files for Printing\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships a BSD pr that differs from GNU pr in header format, column handling, and\n6\t  flag syntax. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gpr,\n7\t  installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n8\t\n9\tgoals:\n10\t  - G1: Paginate text files with headers, footers, and page numbers.\n11\t  - G2: Support multi-column layout and line numbering.\n12\t  - G3: Verify functional parity against gpr via differential testing.\n13\t\n14\trequirements:\n15\t  R1:\n16\t    title: Page layout\n17\t    items:\n18\t      - R1.1:\n19\t          text: Must format input into pages of 66 lines by default (header 5 lines, body 56 lines, footer 5 lines). Each page header shows the date, filename, and page number.\n20\t\n21\t  R2:\n22\t    title: Page options\n23\t    items:\n24\t      - R2.1:\n25\t          text: \"-l N or --length=N must set the page length to N lines. -h HEADER or --header=HEADER must replace the filename in the header.\"\n26\t      - R2.2:\n27\t          text: \"-t or --omit-header must suppress the 5-line header and 5-line footer. -T or --omit-pagination must suppress header/footer and do not pad page bottom.\"\n28\t      - R2.3:\n29\t          text: Must read from FILE arguments or stdin when no file or \"-\" is given.\n30\t\n31\t  R3:\n32\t    title: Multi-column output\n33\t    items:\n34\t      - R3.1:\n35\t          text: \"-COLUMN or --columns=COLUMN must produce multi-column output. Columns are filled down by default. -a or --across fills across instead.\"\n36\t\n37\t  R4:\n38\t    title: Formatting options\n39\t    items:\n40\t      - R4.1:\n41\t          text: \"-n[CHAR[WIDTH]] or --number-lines[=CHAR[WIDTH]] must number output lines. CHAR is the separator (default tab), WIDTH is the number field width (default 5).\"\n42\t      - R4.2:\n43\t          text: \"-o MARGIN or --indent=MARGIN must indent each line by MARGIN spaces. -w WIDTH or --width=WIDTH must set the page width (default 72).\"\n44\t      - R4.3:\n45\t          text: \"-d or --double-space must double-space the output. -s CHAR or --separator=CHAR must use CHAR as the column separator (default tab).\"\n46\t\n47\t  R5:\n48\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n49\t    items:\n50\t      - R5.1:\n51\t          text: Must exit 0 on success. Must exit 1 on any error.\n52\t      - R5.2:\n53\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n54\t\n55\tnon_goals:\n56\t  - cmd/pr does not implement -m (merge files side by side) in this release.\n57\t\n58\tacceptance_criteria:\n59\t  - id: AC1\n60\t    criterion: \"pr on a text file produces paginated output with header, matching gpr.\"\n61\t    traces:\n62\t      - R1.1\n63\t      - R2.3\n64\t  - id: AC2\n65\t    criterion: \"pr -2 produces two-column output, matching gpr -2.\"\n66\t    traces:\n67\t      - R3.1\n68\t  - id: AC3\n69\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gpr passes.\"\n70\t    traces:\n71\t      - R1.1\n72\t      - R3.1\n73\t  - id: AC4\n74\t    criterion: \"cmd/pr compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n75\t    traces:\n76\t      - R1.1\n77\t      - R2.1\n78\t      - R2.2\n79\t      - R2.3\n80\t      - R3.1\n81\t      - R4.1\n82\t      - R4.2\n83\t      - R4.3\n84\t      - R5.1\n85\t      - R5.2\n86\t\n87\tpackage_contract:\n88\t  imports:\n89\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b522e3e-ef6e-4d63-b9a0-d59d924f70f8","uuid":"3c3ea1b5-9926-4bbf-ba60-50ee9feaac36","timestamp":"2026-05-28T17:43:13.119Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5639/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd110-pr.yaml","content":"id: srd110-pr\ntitle: \"cmd/pr: Paginate or Columnate Files for Printing\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships a BSD pr that differs from GNU pr in header format, column handling, and\n  flag syntax. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gpr,\n  installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Paginate text files with headers, footers, and page numbers.\n  - G2: Support multi-column layout and line numbering.\n  - G3: Verify functional parity against gpr via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Page layout\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must format input into pages of 66 lines by default (header 5 lines, body 56 lines, footer 5 lines). Each page header shows the date, filename, and page number.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Page options\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-l N or --length=N must set the page length to N lines. -h HEADER or --header=HEADER must replace the filename in the header.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"-t or --omit-header must suppress the 5-line header and 5-line footer. -T or --omit-pagination must suppress header/footer and do not pad page bottom.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must read from FILE arguments or stdin when no file or \"-\" is given.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Multi-column output\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"-COLUMN or --columns=COLUMN must produce multi-column output. Columns are filled down by default. -a or --across fills across instead.\"\n\n  R4:\n    title: Formatting options\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: \"-n[CHAR[WIDTH]] or --number-lines[=CHAR[WIDTH]] must number output lines. CHAR is the separator (default tab), WIDTH is the number field width (default 5).\"\n      - R4.2:\n          text: \"-o MARGIN or --indent=MARGIN must indent each line by MARGIN spaces. -w WIDTH or --width=WIDTH must set the page width (default 72).\"\n      - R4.3:\n          text: \"-d or --double-space must double-space the output. -s CHAR or --separator=CHAR must use CHAR as the column separator (default tab).\"\n\n  R5:\n    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n    items:\n      - R5.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 on success. Must exit 1 on any error.\n      - R5.2:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/pr does not implement -m (merge files side by side) in this release.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"pr on a text file produces paginated output with header, matching gpr.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.3\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"pr -2 produces two-column output, matching gpr -2.\"\n    traces:\n      - R3.1\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gpr passes.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R3.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/pr compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n      - R5.1\n      - R5.2\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":90,"startLine":1,"totalLines":90}}}
